    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0192" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President to the
                        Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d145-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tunis</hi></placeName>] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-20">20 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the President to Ambassador Steinhardt</p>
                <p>Hope you can come to Cairo either immediately or later. I hope to be there until
                    Saturday November 27 and to be back there about six days later.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d145-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d145-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House, apparently via military channels; forwarded to the
                    Department of State; and forwarded further by the Department, in paraphrase, in
                    telegram 902, November 20, 1943, 4 p.m., to the Legation at Ankara, marked “Most
                    Secret and Personal” and “U. S. Urgent”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
